	('privacypolicy', 'en', 'messages', '<h3>Privacy Policy</h3><p>BeWelcome offers an online place to meet friends, and a chance to meet people in the real world. This Privacy Policy is intended to inform you of BeWelcome\'s policies and practices regarding the collection, use and disclosure of any Personal Information you submit to us through our Website.\r\nBeWelcome ("BeWelcome", "us" or "we") respects the privacy of the visitors to its Website, the home page of which is located at http://www.BeWelcome.org ("Website"). </p><h4>Terms of this disclaimer</h4><p>"Personal Information" is information about you that is personally identifiable to you, like your name, address, e-mail address, or phone number, as well as other non-public information that is associated with the foregoing.\r\n"Anonymous Information" means information that is not associated with or linked to your Personal Information; Anonymous Information does not permit the identification of individual persons. We collect and use Personal Information and Anonymous Information as described in this Privacy Policy. </p><h4>User Consent</h4><p>By submitting Personal Information through our Website, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy and expressly consent to the processing of your Personal Information according to this Privacy Policy. Your Personal Information may be processed by BeWelcome in the country where it was collected as well as other countries (including the United States of America) where laws regarding processing of Personal Information may be less stringent than the laws in your country.</p><h4>General</h4><p>We collect Personal Information that you submit to us voluntarily through our Website.<ul><li> When you register for the BeWelcome network, we will collect your name, e-mail address, your gender, date of birth and post code.</li><li>When you save other Personal Information in your profile we will collect any such information you enter.</li><li>When you enter Personal Information throughout the BeWelcome network using one of the features of the BeWelcome network, for example blogs, groups, or message boards (forum), we will collect any such information you enter ("Publicly Posted Information").</li><li>When you contact us by sending us an e-mail, we will collect your e-mail addresses and any information contained in the e-mail you send us. Once you register with BeWelcome and sign in to our services, you are not anonymous to us. If you are browsing the Website without registering with BeWelcome, you are anonymous to us, but we will collect the information listed below under Personal Information Collected Via Technology.</li></ul></p>\r\n<h4>Use of information</h4><p>Any visitor of the BeWelcome website can view your profile information and photos that you have uploaded to the BeWelcome community. You can control what part of your profile information and photos is visible to visitors of the BeWelcome website and which network of BeWelcome members can see what information. To provide you with some of the features that the BeWelcome community offers to its members, we may use Personal Information that is stored in your profile after you have requested such features, for example to send invitation e-mails to people that you specified as being interested in joining the BeWelcome community. When you decide to view a member\'s profile, we may show that BeWelcome member that you chose to view their profile. If you decide to use certain features of the BeWelcome network (like blogs, groups, message boards and the like), some of the Personal Information you entered into your BeWelcome profile and any information, including Personal Information, that you enter using one of these features, might be used and displayed. BeWelcome members can use the search feature to search for other members by different criteria, like location or interests. The Personal Information that BeWelcome members enter into the BeWelcome profile will be used for these searches. Please be aware that any information that is publicly posted throughout the BeWelcome network can be accessed by every visitor of the Website. BeWelcome may analyse any collected information for its own internal purposes. BeWelcome may use Anonymous Information for any purpose and disclose Anonymous Information in its discretion.</p><h4>Information Sharing and Disclosure</h4><p>BeWelcome does not rent, sell, or share personal information about you with other people or companies except to provide products or services you\'ve requested, when we have your permission, or as otherwise described in this privacy policy.\r\nWe will disclose information in response to subpoenas, court orders, or legal process, or to establish or exercise our legal rights or defend against legal claims. We may disclose information, if we believe it is necessary to investigate, prevent, or take action regarding suspected illegal activities or fraud, situations involving the physical safety of any person, violations of BeWelcome\'s terms of use, or as otherwise required by applicable law. </p>\r\n<h4>Personal Information Collected Via Technology</h4><p>As you navigate the Website, certain information may also be passively collected and stored on our server logs, including your Internet protocol address, browser type, and operating system. We also use Cookies and navigational data like Uniform Resource Locators (URL) to gather information regarding the date and time of your visit and the solutions and information for which you searched and viewed. This type of information is collected to make our services and solutions more useful to you and to tailor the BeWelcome community experience to meet your special interests and needs. If you search the BeWelcome community by using a toolbar that BeWelcome, we may collect Anonymous Information about you automatically, but we will not collect Personal Information.\r\nAn "Internet protocol address" or "IP Address" is a number that is automatically assigned to your computer when you use the Internet. In some cases your IP Address stays the same from browser session to browser session; but if you use a consumer internet access provider, your IP Address probably varies from session to session. We track your IP Address when you login to the Website.\r\n"Cookies" are small pieces of information that a web site sends to your computer\'s hard drive while you are viewing a web site. BeWelcome may use both session Cookies (which expire once you close your web browser) and persistent Cookies (which stay on your computer until you delete them) to provide you with a more personal and interactive experience on the Website. Persistent Cookies can be removed by following your Internet browser help file directions. If you choose to disable Cookies, some areas of the Website may not work properly. Other third parties may place advertisements and cookies on webpages within the BeWelcome network. Other companies and organisations use of their cookies is subject to their own privacy policies, not this one. </p><h4>Your Ability to Edit and Delete Your Account Information and Preferences</h4><p>We reserve the right to send you certain communications relating to the BeWelcome service, such as service announcements, administrative messages and the BeWelcome Newsletter, that are considered part of your BeWelcome account. If you would like to opt out of certain messages, log into BeWelcome and go to your account settings by clicking the account link in the top right hand corner. On that page you can edit your preferences. If you would like to delete your account, log into BeWelcome, Go to My account > Edit my profile in the left column there\'s a \'delete my profile\' link, click this, then fill in some optional data in the form, and check the checkbox below, finally press the \'submit query\'.</p> <h4>Confidentiality and Security</h4><p>We limit access to personal information about you to employees and third parties who we reasonably believe need access to that information to provide products or services to you or in order to do their jobs.\r\nWe have physical, electronic, and procedural safeguards to protect personal information about you and your BeWelcome account information is protected by a password that you select. BeWelcome uses industry-standard SSL encryption in certain areas of the Website to protect data transmissions. However, no company, including BeWelcome, can fully eliminate security risks associated with Personal Information. </p><h4>Other Sites</h4><p>Our provision of a link to any other website or location is for your convenience and does not signify our endorsement of such other website or location or its contents. We have no control over, do not review, and cannot be responsible for these outside websites or their content. Please be aware that the terms of our Privacy Policy does not apply to these outside websites.</p><h4>Contact Us</h4><p>Should you have any questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us:\r\n<address>BeVolunteer 19 rue de Paris 35500 Vitré FRANCE</address> </p><h4>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h4><p>BeWelcome may update this policy from time to time. We will notify you about significant changes in the way we treat Personal Information by sending a notice to the primary email address specified in your BeWelcome account or by placing a prominent notice on our Website. If you object to any such changes, you must cease using our Website. Continued use of our Website following notice of any such changes shall indicate your acknowledgement of such changes and agreement to be bound by the terms and conditions of such changes. </p><p>This Policy was last updated in June 2012.</p>', '2008-02-10 11:40:18', '2019-04-23 18:16:49', '2012-06-19 15:50:51', 'yes', 'Please translate this very carefuly, this is the privacy police as displayed on the page http://www.bewelcome.org/privacy', 7, NULL, 554),
	('privacypolicy', 'hy', 'messages', '<p>&nbsp;</p><p>Privacy Policy</p><p>բիվելքմ offers an online place to meet friends, and a chance to meet people in the real world. This Privacy Policy is intended to inform you of BeWelcome\'s policies and practices regarding the collection, use and disclosure of any Personal Information you submit to us through our Website. BeWelcome ("BeWelcome", "us" or "we") respects the privacy of the visitors to its Website, the home page of which is located at <a href="http://www.bewelcome.org/">http://www.BeWelcome.org</a> ("Website").</p><p>Terms of this disclaimer</p><p>"Personal Information" is information about you that is personally identifiable to you, like your name, address, e-mail address, or phone number, as well as other non-public information that is associated with the foregoing. "Anonymous Information" means information that is not associated with or linked to your Personal Information; Anonymous Information does not permit the identification of individual persons. We collect and use Personal Information and Anonymous Information as described in this Privacy Policy.</p><p>User Consent</p><p>By submitting Personal Information through our Website, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy and expressly consent to the processing of your Personal Information according to this Privacy Policy. Your Personal Information may be processed by BeWelcome in the country where it was collected as well as other countries (including the United States of America) where laws regarding processing of Personal Information may be less stringent than the laws in your country.</p><p>General</p><p>We collect Personal Information that you submit to us voluntarily through our Website.</p><ul><li>When you register for the BeWelcome network, we will collect your name, e-mail address, your gender, date of birth and post code.</li><li>When you save other Personal Information in your profile we will collect any such information you enter.</li><li>When you enter Personal Information throughout the BeWelcome network using one of the features of the BeWelcome network, for example blogs, groups, or message boards (forum), we will collect any such information you enter ("Publicly Posted Information").</li><li>When you contact us by sending us an e-mail, we will collect your e-mail addresses and any information contained in the e-mail you send us. Once you register with BeWelcome and sign in to our services, you are not anonymous to us. If you are browsing the Website without registering with BeWelcome, you are anonymous to us, but we will collect the information listed below under Personal Information Collected Via Technology.</li></ul><p>Use of information</p><p>Any visitor of the BeWelcome website can view your profile information and photos that you have uploaded to the BeWelcome community. You can control what part of your profile information and photos is visible to visitors of the BeWelcome website and which network of BeWelcome members can see what information. To provide you with some of the features that the BeWelcome community offers to its members, we may use Personal Information that is stored in your profile after you have requested such features, for example to send invitation e-mails to people that you specified as being interested in joining the BeWelcome community. When you decide to view a member\'s profile, we may show that BeWelcome member that you chose to view their profile. If you decide to use certain features of the BeWelcome network (like blogs, groups, message boards and the like), some of the Personal Information you entered into your BeWelcome profile and any information, including Personal Information, that you enter using one of these features, might be used and displayed. BeWelcome members can use the search feature to search for other members by different criteria, like location or interests. The Personal Information that BeWelcome members enter into the BeWelcome profile will be used for these searches. Please be aware that any information that is publicly posted throughout the BeWelcome network can be accessed by every visitor of the Website. BeWelcome may analyse any collected information for its own internal purposes. BeWelcome may use Anonymous Information for any purpose and disclose Anonymous Information in its discretion.</p><p>Information Sharing and Disclosure</p><p>BeWelcome does not rent, sell, or share personal information about you with other people or companies except to provide products or services you\'ve requested, when we have your permission, or as otherwise described in this privacy policy. We will disclose information in response to subpoenas, court orders, or legal process, or to establish or exercise our legal rights or defend against legal claims. We may disclose information, if we believe it is necessary to investigate, prevent, or take action regarding suspected illegal activities or fraud, situations involving the physical safety of any person, violations of BeWelcome\'s terms of use, or as otherwise required by applicable law.</p><p>Personal Information Collected Via Technology</p><p>As you navigate the Website, certain information may also be passively collected and stored on our server logs, including your Internet protocol address, browser type, and operating system. We also use Cookies and navigational data like Uniform Resource Locators (URL) to gather information regarding the date and time of your visit and the solutions and information for which you searched and viewed. This type of information is collected to make our services and solutions more useful to you and to tailor the BeWelcome community experience to meet your special interests and needs. If you search the BeWelcome community by using a toolbar that BeWelcome, we may collect Anonymous Information about you automatically, but we will not collect Personal Information. An "Internet protocol address" or "IP Address" is a number that is automatically assigned to your computer when you use the Internet. In some cases your IP Address stays the same from browser session to browser session; but if you use a consumer internet access provider, your IP Address probably varies from session to session. We track your IP Address when you login to the Website. "Cookies" are small pieces of information that a web site sends to your computer\'s hard drive while you are viewing a web site. BeWelcome may use both session Cookies (which expire once you close your web browser) and persistent Cookies (which stay on your computer until you delete them) to provide you with a more personal and interactive experience on the Website. Persistent Cookies can be removed by following your Internet browser help file directions. If you choose to disable Cookies, some areas of the Website may not work properly. Other third parties may place advertisements and cookies on webpages within the BeWelcome network. Other companies and organisations use of their cookies is subject to their own privacy policies, not this one.</p><p>Your Ability to Edit and Delete Your Account Information and Preferences</p><p>We reserve the right to send you certain communications relating to the BeWelcome service, such as service announcements, administrative messages and the BeWelcome Newsletter, that are considered part of your BeWelcome account. If you would like to opt out of certain messages, log into BeWelcome and go to your account settings by clicking the account link in the top right hand corner. On that page you can edit your preferences. If you would like to delete your account, log into BeWelcome, Go to My account &gt; Edit my profile in the left column there\'s a \'delete my profile\' link, click this, then fill in some optional data in the form, and check the checkbox below, finally press the \'submit query\'.</p><p>Confidentiality and Security</p><p>We limit access to personal information about you to employees and third parties who we reasonably believe need access to that information to provide products or services to you or in order to do their jobs. We have physical, electronic, and procedural safeguards to protect personal information about you and your BeWelcome account information is protected by a password that you select. BeWelcome uses industry-standard SSL encryption in certain areas of the Website to protect data transmissions. However, no company, including BeWelcome, can fully eliminate security risks associated with Personal Information.</p><p>Other Sites</p><p>Our provision of a link to any other website or location is for your convenience and does not signify our endorsement of such other website or location or its contents. We have no control over, do not review, and cannot be responsible for these outside websites or their content. Please be aware that the terms of our Privacy Policy does not apply to these outside websites.</p><p>Contact Us</p><p>Should you have any questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us:</p><p>BeVolunteer 19 rue de Paris 35500 Vitré FRANCE Changes to this Privacy Policy</p><p>BeWelcome may update this policy from time to time. We will notify you about significant changes in the way we treat Personal Information by sending a notice to the primary email address specified in your BeWelcome account or by placing a prominent notice on our Website. If you object to any such changes, you must cease using our Website. Continued use of our Website following notice of any such changes shall indicate your acknowledgement of such changes and agreement to be bound by the terms and conditions of such changes.</p><p>This Policy was last updated in June 2012.</p>', '2025-09-22 04:37:17', '2025-09-22 04:37:17', '2025-09-22 04:37:17', 'no', '', 5, NULL, 519603),
	('privacypolicy', 'it', 'messages', '<h3>Informativa sul trattamento dei dati personali</h3><p>\r\nBeWelcome offre uno spazio online per trovare amici e l\'opportunità di incontrare persone nella vita reale. Questa informativa sul trattamento dei dati personali intende informarti sulle politiche e le procedure riguardanti la raccolta, l’uso e la comunicazione di qualsiasi informazione personale che ci comunichi tramite il nostro sito. BeWelcome (di seguito “BeWelcome” oppure “noi”) rispetta la privacy dei visitatori di questo sito, e la schermata principale si trova qui http://www.BeWelcome.org (di seguito, "sito web").</p><h4>\r\nDichiarazione di non responsabilità</h4><p>“Informazioni personali” sono le informazioni riguardanti la tua persona e che sono direttamente identificabili con te, come il tuo nome, indirizzo, email, o numero di telefono, così come qualsiasi altra informazione privata associabile alle precedenti.\r\n“Informazioni anonime” sono le informazioni che non sono associate o collegate alle tue informazioni personali; le informazioni anonime non permettono l’identificazione di singoli individui.\r\nRaccogliamo e usiamo le informazioni personali e le informazioni anonime secondo quanto descritto in questa informativa.</p><h4>\r\nConsenso dell’utente</h4><p>Dando le tue informazioni personali tramite il nostro sito, accetti i termini di questa informativa sulla privacy e acconsenti espressamente al trattamento dei tuoi dati personali come regolato dalla stessa informativa. Le tue informazioni personali potranno essere trattate da BeWelcome sia nel paese dove sono state raccolte, sia in altri paesi (inclusi gli Stati Uniti d’America), dove le leggi sul trattamento dei dati personali possono essere meno restrittive rispetto a quelle del tuo paese.</p><h4>\r\nInformazioni generali</h4><p>Raccogliamo le informazioni personali che ci trasmetti volontariamente tramite il sito.<ul><li>Quando ti registri su BeWelcome, raccogliamo il tuo nome e indirizzo email, il tuo genere, la tua data di nascita ed il CAP.</li><li>Quando salvi altre informazioni personali nel tuo profilo, raccogliamo tali informazioni.</li><li>Quando immetti informazioni personali tramite BeWelcome usando gli strumenti del sito, per esempio blog, gruppi, o il forum, raccoglieremo le informazioni che immetterai ("Informazioni postate pubblicamente").</li><li>Quando ci contatti per email, raccogliamo l’informazione relativa al tuo indirizzo email e altre informazioni che hai inserito nel messaggio di posta elettronica che ci hai mandato. Quando ti registri su BeWelcome e i suoi servizi, non sei anonimo per noi. Se invece navighi sul sito senza essere registrato su BeWelcome sei anonimo, però verranno raccolte le informazioni di seguito definite come "Informazioni personali raccolte tramite tecnologia".</li></ul></p>\r\n<h4>Uso delle informazioni</h4><p>Ogni visitatore del sito di BeWelcome può vedere le informazioni del tuo profilo e le foto che hai caricato nella comunità di BeWelcome. Puoi controllare tu stesso quali parti del tuo profilo e quali foto vuoi rendere visibili ai visitatori e quali invece solo ai membri di BeWelcome. Per metterti a disposizione alcuni degli strumenti che BeWelcome offre ai suoi membri, potremmo usare informazioni personali salvate nel tuo profilo nel momento in cui richiedi di usare tali strumenti, per esempio per mandare email d’invito a persone che tu segnali come interessati ad iscriversi a BeWelcome. Quando decidi di vedere il profilo di un membro, mostreremo a tale membro che hai visitato il suo profilo. Se deciderai di usare alcuni strumenti della rete BeWelcome (blog, gruppi, forum e simili), alcune delle tue informazioni personali che hai inserito nel profilo e tutte le informazioni, incluse quelle personali, che inserisci utilizzando uno di questi strumenti, potranno essere usate e visualizzate. I membri di BeWelcome possono usare lo strumento di ricerca per trovare altri membri utilizzando vari criteri, come la località o gli interessi. Le informazioni personali che i membri di BeWelcome inseriscono nel loro profilo saranno usate per queste ricerche. Per favore, tieni presente che tutte le informazioni che sono inserite in modo pubblico sulla rete BeWelcome possono essere visualizzate da qualsiasi visitatore del sito. BeWelcome potrà analizzare qualsiasi informazione raccolta per scopi interni. BeWelcome potrà usare le informazioni anonime per qualsiasi scopo e trattare le informazioni anonime a sua discrezione.</p><h4>Condivisione e divulgazione delle informazioni</h4><p>BeWelcome non affitta, vende o condivide informazioni personali relative alla tua persona con altre persone o imprese, eccetto che per mettere a disposizione prodotti e servizi che hai richiesto, quando abbiamo il tuo esplicito permesso, o come altrimenti descritto in questa informativa. Comunicheremo i dati in risposta a citazioni in giudizio, ordini di tribunali o processi legali, oppure per esercitare i nostri diritti legali o difenderci da azioni legali. Potremmo usare le informazioni se reputiamo sia necessario per investigare, prevenire, o contrastare attività sospettate di essere illegali o frodi, situazioni che coinvolgono la sicurezza fisica di qualsiasi persona, violazioni dei Termini d’uso di BeWelcome, o come altrimenti richiesto dalle vigenti leggi.</p>\r\n<h4>Informazioni personali raccolte tramite la tecnologia</h4><p>Mentre navighi per il sito, alcune informazioni possono essere raccolte in modo passivo e salvate nei log sul server, come ad esempio il tuo indirizzo di protocollo internet, il tipo di browser ed il sistema operativo. Usiamo anche cookie e dati sulla navigazione come Uniform Resource Locators (URL) per raccogliere informazioni riguardo l’ora e la data della tua visita e in merito a quali informazioni hai cercato e visualizzato. Questo tipo di informazioni sono raccolte per migliorare i nostri servizi e per adattare al meglio la comunità e la rete di BeWelcome ai tuoi interessi e alle tue esigenze. Se effettui una ricerca nella comunità di BeWelcome, le tue informazioni anonime potranno essere raccolte automaticamente, però non verranno raccolte le informazioni personali.\r\nUn “indirizzo di protocollo internet”  o "indirizzo IP" è il numero automaticamente assegnato al tuo computer quando usi internet. In alcuni casi il tuo indirizzo IP rimane uguale ogni volta che ti colleghi, ma se usi un internet provider è probabile che il tuo indirizzo vari di volta in volta. Teniamo traccia del tuo indirizzo IP quando accedi al sito.\r\n“Cookies” sono piccoli pezzi d’informazione che un sito internet invia al disco fisso del tuo computer mentre stai navigando. BeWelcome usa sia cookie validi per una sessione (che vengono cancellati quando chiudi il browser), sia cookie persistenti (che rimangono sul tuo computer fino a quando non li cancelli) per poterti offrire un’esperienza più personale e interattiva sul sito. I Cookie persistenti possono essere cancellati seguendo le istruzioni del tuo browser. Se scegli di disattivare i Cookie, alcune aree del sito potrebbero non funzionare correttamente. Servizi di terze parti potrebbero inserire cookie e pubblicità su pagine del sito BeWelcome. L’uso del Cookie da parte di altri organizzazioni o imprese è soggetto alla loro informativa sulla privacy, non alla nostra.</p><h4>\r\nLa possibilità di modificare e cancellare le informazioni e preferenze del tuo account</h4><p>Ci riserviamo il diritto di mandarti alcune comunicazioni relative al servizio di BeWelcome, come annunci di servizio, messaggi amministrativi e il notiziario di BeWelcome; tali comunicazioni sono considerate parte del tuo account di BeWelcome. Se non vuoi però ricevere alcuni messaggi, accedi al sito BeWelcome e vai alle preferenze del tuo account selezionando il link in alto a destra. Su tale pagina puoi modificare le tue preferenze. Se vuoi cancellare il tuo profilo, accedi a BeWelcome, vai su Il mio account > Modifica profilo: nella colonna a sinistra c\'è il collegamento "cancella profilo". Puoi compilare alcuni dati opzionali, poi spunta la casella sottostante e infine seleziona "cancella profilo".\r\n</p><h4>Confidenzialità e sicurezza</h4><p>Limitiamo l’accesso alle informazioni personali relative alla tua persona solo a quelle persone che lavorano con e per noi e a quelle parti terze che crediamo abbiano ragionevole motivo di accedere a tali informazioni per poterti offrire prodotti e servizi e fare il loro lavoro.\r\nOffriamo sicurezza fisica, elettronica e procedurale per proteggere le informazioni personali riguardanti la tua persona e il tuo account BeWelcome è protetto da una password scelta da te. BeWelcome usa lo standard di crittografia SSL in certe aree del sito per proteggere la trasmissione dati. Comunque nessuna organizzazione, compresa BeWelcome, può eliminare tutti i rischi connessi alla sicurezza delle Informazioni personali.</p><h4>Altri siti</h4><p>Ogni link ad altri siti è postato per tua comodità e non implica la nostra approvazione o appoggio rispetto a tali siti o ai loro contenuti. Non abbiamo nessun controllo e non possiamo essere responsabili dei contenuti di questi siti esterni e dei loro contenuti. Tieni presente che i termini della presente Informativa sulla Privacy non si applicano ai siti esterni.</p><h4>Contattaci</h4><p>Se dovessi avere domande o commenti in merito a questa Informativa sulla Privacy, contattaci:<address>BeVolunteer 19 rue de Paris 35500 Vitré FRANCE</address> </p><h4>Modifiche a questa Informativa sulla Privacy</h4><p>BeWelcome potrà modificare questa informativa. Ti informeremo di cambiamenti significativi sul trattamento dei dati personali mandando un messaggio all’indirizzo email che hai indicato come principale sul tuo account BeWelcome o pubblicando un annuncio ben visibile sul sito. Se sei contrario ad una qualunque di tali modifiche, devi cessare di usare il sito. L\'uso del sito successivo all’annuncio delle modiche indica che sei a conoscenza delle modifiche effettuate e che accetti di essere soggetto ai termini e condizioni previsti da tali modifiche.</p><p>Questa informativa è stata modificata l\'ultima volta nel giugno 2012.</p>', '2008-05-02 18:21:10', '2020-12-08 14:21:39', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'yes', '', 7, NULL, 160610),
	('privacypolicy', 'nl', 'messages', '<h3>Privacybeleid</h3>\r\n<p>BeWelcome biedt een plaats online om vrienden te ontmoeten en een mogelijkheid om mensen te ontmoeten in de echte wereld.  Dit privacybeleid dient ertoe je te informeren over het beleid en de gebruiken van BeWelcome i.v.m. het verzamelen, gebruiken en onthullen van persoonlijke informatie die je ons via de website laat toekomen. BeWelcome (“BeWelcome”, “wij” of “ons”) respecteert de privacy van bezoekers van de website, waarvan de thuispagina te vinden is op http://www.BeWelcome.org (“Website”).</p>\r\n<h4>Terminologie</h4>\r\n<p>“Persoonlijke Informatie” is informatie over u, waarmee u geïdentificeerd kan worden, zoals uw naam, adres, e-mailadres, telefoonnummer of andere niet-publieke informatie die daarmee verband houdt.  “Anonieme Informatie” betekent informatie die niet geassocieerd of verbonden is met uw Persoonlijke Informatie; het is niet mogelijk op basis van Anonieme Informatie individuele personen te identificeren.  Wij verzamelen en gebruiken Persoonlijke Informatie en Anonieme Informatie zoals beschreven in dit Privacybeleid.</p>\r\n<h4>Gebruikersinstemming</h4>\r\n<p>Door Persoonlijke Informatie te verzenden via onze website, gaat u akkoord met de voorwaarden van dit privacybeleid en stemt u expliciet in met het verwerken van uw Persoonlijke Informatie volgens dit privacybeleid.  Uw Persoonlijke Informatie kan door BeWelcome verwerkt worden in het land waar deze werd verzameld, maar ook in andere landen (inclusief de VSA) waar de wetten met betrekking tot het verwerken van Persoonlijke Informatie minder strikt zijn dan in uw land.</p>\r\n<h4>Algemeen</h4>\r\n<p>We verzamelen Persoonlijke Informatie die u vrijwillig via onze website verstuurt.\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Als u zich registreert voor het BeWelcome-netwerk, verzamelen we uw naam, e-mailadres, geslacht, geboortedatum en postcode.</li>\r\n<li>Als u andere Persoonlijke Informatie in uw profiel opslaat, zullen we deze allemaal verzamelen.</li>\r\n<li>Als u Persoonlijke Informatie in het BeWelcome-netwerk via één van de mogelijkheden als blogs, groepen of discussiegroepen (het forum) invoert, zullen we deze verzamelen (“Publiekelijk Geposte Informatie”).</li>\r\n<li>Als u ons contacteert door een e-mail te sturen, verzamelen we uw e-mailadres en andere informatie in de e-mail die u ons stuurt.  Eens je geregistreerd bent bij BeWelcome en u aanmeldt voor onze diensten, bent u niet meer anoniem voor ons.  Als u op de website komt zonder te registreren bij BeWelcome, bent u anoniem voor ons, maar zullen we de informatie verzamelen zoals hieronder opgesomd onder Persoonlijke Informatie Verzameld door Technologie.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n<h4>Gebruik van informatie</h4>\r\n<p>Elke bezoeker van de website van BeWelcom kan uw profielinformatie en de foto’s die u hebt geüpload naar de BeWelcome-gemeenschap zien.  U hebt er controle over welke delen van je profielinformatie en foto’s zichtbaar zijn voor bezoekers van de website van BeWelcome en welk netwerk van de leden van BeWelcome welke informatie kunnen zien.  Om u van enkele van de mogelijkheden die de gemeenschap van BeWelcome aan zijn leden aanbiedt, te kunnen voorzien, kunnen we Persoonlijke Informatie die in uw profiel is opgeslagen, gebruiken, nadat u zulke mogelijkheden hebt aangevraagd; bijvoorbeeld het sturen van uitnodigings-e-mails naar mensen die u aangeeft als geïnteresseerd in het toetreden tot de gemeenschap van BeWelcome.  Als u besluit om het profiel van een lid te bekijken, kunnen we dit lid van BeWelcome tonen dat u haar/zijn profiel wil zien.  Als u besluit om bepaalde mogelijkheden van het netwerk van BeWelcome te gebruiken (zoals blogs, groepen, prikborden en dergelijke), kan sommige Persoonlijke Informatie die u in uw profiel van BeWelcome hebt ingevoerd en informatie, waaronder Persoonlijke Informatie, die u invoert met gebruikmaking van één van deze mogelijkheden, gebruikt en getoond worden.  Leden van BeWelcome kunnen de zoekfunctie gebruiken om naar andere leden te zoeken met verschillende criteria, zoals locatie en interesses.  De Persoonlijke Informatie die leden van BeWelcome in hun profiel bij BeWelcome invoeren, zal gebruikt worden voor deze zoekopdrachten.  Wees u er alstublieft van bewust dat alle informatie die publiekelijk geplaatst wordt over het hele netwerk van BeWelcome toegankelijk is voor elke bezoeker van de website.  BeWelcome kan alle verzamelde informatie analyseren for intern gebruik.  BeWelcome kan Anonieme Informatie gebruiken voor elke doel en naar eigen inzicht Anonieme Informatie bekend maken.</p>\r\n<h4>Delen en vrijgeven van informatie</h4>\r\n<p>BeWelcome verhuurt, verkoopt of deelt geen persoonlijke informatie over jou met andere mensen of bedrijven behalve om producten of diensten te leveren die je zelf hebt aangevraagd, als we daar jouw toestemming voor hebben, of zoals elders in dit privacybeleid beschreven.\r\nWe zullen informatie vrijgeven in antwoord op dagvaardingen, gerechtsorders, of gerechtsprocessen; of om onze rechten te vrijwaren of uit te oefenen; of om ons te verdedigen in rechtszaken.  Als wij denken dat het nodig is voor het onderzoeken van, voorkomen van, of in actie komen tegen gevallen van verdachte illegale activiteiten of fraude, situaties waarin de fysieke veiligheid van een persoon in gevaar komt, inbreuken op de gebruiksvoorwaarden van BeWelcome, of als vereist door toepasselijk recht, kunnen wij informatie vrijgeven.</p>\r\n<h4>Persoonlijke informatie verzameld via technologie</h4>\r\n<p>Terwijl je de website gebruikt, kan er bepaalde informatie op een passieve manier verzameld en bewaard worden in onze serverlogboeken; daaronder je IP-adres, browsertype en besturingssysteem.  We gebruiken ook cookies en gegevens over je navigeergedrag zoals URL’s om informatie te verzamelen over de datum en tijd van je bezoek en de diensten en informatie waar je naar gezocht hebt en die je bekeken hebt.  Dit soort informatie verzamelen we om onze diensten bruikbaarder en nuttiger te maken, om je ervaring bij de BeWelcome-gemeenschap beter aan te passen aan jouw wensen en interesses.  Als je in de BW-gemeenschap zoekt met een zoekbalk van BeWelcome, kunnen we anonieme informatie over jou automatisch verzamelen, maar zullen we geen persoonlijke informatie verzamelen.\r\nEen IP-adres (Internet-Protocol-adres) is een nummer dat automatisch aan je computer wordt toegewezen als je het internet gebruikt.  In sommige gevallen blijft je IP-adres van keer tot keer hetzelfde, maar als je een internetprovider thuis gebruikt, verandert je IP-adres waarschijnlijk van keer tot keer.  We houden je IP-adres bij als je je aanmeldt op de website.\r\n“Cookies” zijn kleine stukjes informatie, die een website naar de harde schijf van je computer stuurt terwijl je naar de website kijkt.  BeWelcome kan zowel sessiecookies (die verlopen zodra je je browser sluit) als blijvende cookies (die op je computer blijven totdat je ze verwijdert) gebruiken, om je een persoonlijkere en interactievere ervaring aan te bieden op de website.  Blijvende cookies kunnen verwijderd worden volgens de instructies in de hulpbestanden van je browser.  Als je ervoor kiest om cookies uit te schakelen, kunnen sommige delen van de site niet goed werken.  Andere derde partijen kunnen advertenties en cookies op pagina’s binnen het netwerk van BeWelcome plaatsen.  Het gebruik van cookies door andere bedrijven en organisaties valt onder hun privacybeleid, niet het deze.</p>\r\n<h4>Mogelijkheden om je accountinformatie en -voorkeuren te bewerken en verwijderen</h4>\r\n<p>We behouden ons het recht voor, je bepaalde informatie te sturen in verband met de dienst van BeWelcome, zoals dienstmededelingen, administratieve berichten en de nieuwsbrief van BeWelcome.  Dit wordt beschouwd als deel van je account bij BeWelcome.  Als je je voor bepaalde berichten wil uitschrijven, meld je dan aan bij BeWelcome en ga naar je accountinstellingen door op de link te klikken in de rechterbovenhoek.  Op die pagina kan je je voorkeuren bewerken.  Als je je account wil verwijderen, meld je aan bij BeWelcome, ga naar Mijn account → Mijn profiel bewerken; in de linkerkolom is er een link ‘Mijn profiel verwijderen’.  Klik hierop, vul enkele optionele gegevens in in het formulier en vink het vakje eronder aan.  Klik ten slotte op de knop ‘Aanvraag verzenden’.</p>\r\n<h4>Vertrouwelijkheid en veiligheid</h4>\r\n<p>We beperken toegang tot uw persoonlijke informatie tot medewerkers en derde partijen waarvan we het aannemelijk vinden dat zij toegang tot die informatie nodig hebben om je producten of diensten aan te bieden of om hun werk te kunnen doen.\r\nWe hebben fysieke, elektronische en procedurele veiligheidsmaatregelen om je persoonlijke informatie te beschermen.  Je accountinformatie bij BeWelcome is beschermd door een wachtwoord dat je zelf kiest.  BeWelcome gebruikt SSL-encryptie volgens industriestandaarden in bepaalde delen van de website om gegevensoverdracht te beveiligen.  Maar geen enkel bedrijf, ook niet BeWelcome, kan veiligheidsrisico’s die met persoonlijke informatie te maken hebben volledig uitsluiten.</p>\r\n<h4>Andere sites</h4>\r\n<p>Als wij verwijzingen naar andere sites of locaties aanbieden, dan is dat enkel voor jouw gemak; dit betekent niet dat wij deze website of locatie, of hun inhouden, ondersteunen. Deze externe websites en hun inhoud vallen buiten onze controle, we kijken ze niet na en kunnen er dus niet verantwoordelijk voor gehouden worden.  Wees je ervan bewust dat ons privacybeleid voor deze externe websites niet geldt.</p>\r\n<h4>Contactmogelijkheden</h4>\r\n<p>Als je vragen of opmerkingen hebt betreffende dit privacybeleid, kan je ons contacteren:\r\n<address>BeVolunteer 19 rue de Paris 35500 Vitré FRANCE</address> </p>\r\n<h4>Wijzigingen aan dit privacybeleid</h4>\r\n<p>BeWelcome kan dit privacybeleid van tijd tot tijd bijwerken.  We zullen je waarschuwen van beduidende wijzigingen in hoe we persoonlijke informatie behandelen door een bericht te sturen naar het primaire e-mailadres dat in je account bij BeWelcome is opgegeven, of door een prominente aankondiging op onze website te plaatsen.  Als je bezwaar maakt tegen zulke veranderingen, moet je ophouden onze website te gebruiken.  Blijvend gebruik van onze website nadat deze aankondiging van zulke wijzigingen is gebeurd, geeft aan dat je het eens bent met de wijzigingen and dat je de voorwaarden van zulke wijzigingen aanvaardt.</p>\r\n<p>Dit beleidsdocument werd laatst bijgewerkt in juni 2012.</p>', '2012-07-01 09:20:46', '2019-04-23 18:16:49', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'yes', '', 5, NULL, 21169),
	('privacypolicy', 'pt', 'messages', '<h3>Política de Privacidade</h3><p>O BeWelcome disponibiliza um sítio para encontrar amigos online e a oportunidade de conhecer pessoas no mundo real. Esta Política de Privacidade pretende dar-lhe a conhecer as políticas do BeWelcome e as práticas que dizem respeito à recolha, utilização e disponibilização de qualquer Informação Pessoal que nos envie através do nosso site.\r\nO BeWelcome ("BeWelcome" ou "nós") respeita a privacidade de quem visita o seu website, cuja página principal se localiza em http://www.BeWelcome.org ("Website"). </p><h4>Termos usados neste texto</h4><p>"Informação Pessoal" é a informação sobre si que o/a identifica pessoalmente, como o seu nome, morada, endereço de correio eletrónico ou número de telefone, assim como qualquer outra informação não pública que lhe esteja associada.\r\n"Informação Anónima" diz respeito a informação que não está associada à sua Informação Pessoal; a Informação Anónima não permite a identificação de pessoas individualmente. Recolhemos e usamos Informação Pessoal e Informação Anónima de acordo com os termos descritos nesta Política de Privacidade. </p><h4>Permissão do Utilizador</h4><p>Ao submeter Informação Pessoal através do nosso Website, concorda com as condições desta Política de Privacidade e autoriza expressamente o processamento da sua Informação Pessoal de acordo com esta Política de Privacidade. A sua Informação Pessoal pode ser processada pelo BeWelcome no país onde foi recolhida assim como noutros países (incluindo os Estados Unidos da América) onde as leis referentes ao tratamento de Informação Pessoal podem ser menos restritivas que as do seu país.</p><h4>Geral</h4><p>Recolhemos Informação Pessoal que nos envia de forma voluntária através do nosso Website.<ul><li> Quando se regista na rede BeWelcome, recolhemos o seu nome, endereço de correio eletrónico, o seu sexo, data de nascimento e código postal.</li><li>Quando grava outra Informação Pessoal no seu perfil recolhemos a informação que escrever.</li><li>Quando envia Informação Pessoal através da rede BeWelcome usando uma das funcionalidades da rede BeWelcome, por exemplo, blogs, grupos ou fóruns, recolhemos essa informação ("Informação Enviada Publicamente").</li><li>Quando nos contacta enviando uma mensagem de correio eletrónico, guardamos o seu endereço de correio eletrónico e qualquer informação contida na mensagem que nos enviar. Assim que se inscreve no BeWelcome e acede aos nossos serviços, não é anónimo para nós. Se estiver a navegar no Website sem se ter inscrito no BeWelcome é anónimo para nós mas iremos na mesma recolher a informação indicada abaixo na secção Informação Pessoal Recolhida de forma Tecnológica.</li></ul></p> \r\n<h4>Utilização dada à Informação</h4><p>Qualquer visitante do BeWelcome pode ver a sua informação de perfil assim como fotos que enviou para a comunidade BeWelcome. Pode controlar que informação do seu perfil e fotos são visíveis a visitantes do website BeWelcome e que parte dos membros BeWelcome tem acesso a que informação. Para lhe fornecer algumas das funcionalidades que a comunidade BeWelcome oferece aos seus membros, podemos usar Informação Pessoal guardada no seu perfil após ter pedido essas funcionalidades, por exemplo, enviar mensagens de correio eletrónico a pessoas que queira convidar a juntar-se à rede BeWelcome. Quando decide ver o perfil de um membro, podemos indicar a esse membro que viu o seu perfil. Se decidir usar certas funcionalidades da rede BeWelcome (como blogs, grupos, fóruns e afins) alguma da Informação Pessoal que inserir no seu perfil e qualquer informação, incluindo Informação Pessoal, que enviar através de uma dessas funcionalidades, pode ser usadas e exibida. Os membros do BeWelcome podem usar funcionalidades de pesquisa para procurar outros membros por vários critérios como localização ou interesses. A Informação Pessoal que os membros BeWelcome deixem no seu perfil pode ser usada nestas pesquisas. Tenha em atenção que qualquer informação que seja publicada na rede BeWelcome pode ser acedida por qualquer visitante do Website. O BeWelcome pode analisar qualquer informação recolhida de acordo com os seus próprios objetivos internos. O BeWelcome pode usar Informação Anónima para qualquer objetivo e divulgar Informação Anónima segundo a sua própria discrição. </p><h4>Partilha e Divulgação de Informação</h4><p>O BeWelcome não aluga, vende ou partilha informação sobre si com outras pessoas ou empresas excepto para oferecer produtos ou serviços que tenha pedido, sempre com a sua permissão ou de acordo com as condições descritas nesta Política de Privacidade.\r\nDivulgaremos informação em resposta a intimações, ordens do tribunal ou processos legais, ou para estabelecer ou exercer os nossos direitos legais ou nos defendermos contra alegações legais. Podemos divulgar informação se acreditarmos ser necessária para investigar, prevenir ou agir contra atividades suspeitas de ilegalidade ou frause, situações envolvendo a segurança física de qualquer pessoa, violações das Condições de Utilização do BeWelcome ou outros motivos impostos pela lei aplicável. </p> \r\n<h4>Informação Pessoal Recolhida de forma Tecnológica</h4><p>À medida que navega no Website, alguma informação pode também ser recolhida de forma passiva e armazenada nos nossos servidores, incluindo o seu protocolo de acesso à Internet, tipo de browser e sistema operativo. Também usamos Cookies e dados de navegação como Uniform Resource Locators (URL) para recolher informação relativamente à data e hora da sua visita e as soluções e informação que pesquisou e viu. Este tipo de informação é recolhido para tornar os nossos serviços e soluções mais úteis e para adequar a experiência da comunidade BeWelcome ao encontro dos seus interesses e necessidades especiais. Se procurar na comunidade BeWelcome usando uma barra de ferramentas do BeWelcome, podemos recolher automaticamente Informação Anónima sobre si mas não iremos recolher Informação Pessoal. Um "Endereço de Protocolo Internet" ou "Endereço IP" é um número automaticamente atribuído ao seu computador quando usa a Internet. Em alguns casos o seu Endereço IP permanece o mesmo entre sessões; mas se usa um fornecedor de acesso à internet doméstico o seu Endereço IP provavelmente varia de uma sessão para a outra. Registamos o seu Endereço IP sempre que se autentica no nosso Website.\r\n"Cookies" são pequenos pedaços de informação que um website envia para o disco do seu computador enquanto visita um website. O BeWelcome pode usar Cookies de sessão (que perdem a validade quando fecha o seu browser) e Cookies Persistentes (que ficam no seu computador até que os apague) para fornecer uma experiência mais personalizada e interativa no nosso Website. Cookies Persistentes podem ser removidos seguindo as indicações do seu browser. Se optar por desativar os Cookies algumas áreas do site podem não funcionar corretamente. Entidades terceiras podem colocar anúncios e cookies em páginas da rede BeWelcome. O uso que outras companhias e organizações fazem das cookies está sujeito às suas próprias Políticas de Privacidade, não a esta. </p><h4>Possibilidade de Alterar e Apagar Informação e Preferencias da Sua Conta</h4><p>Reservamo-nos o direito de lhe enviar certas comunicações relacionadas com o serviço BeWelcome, tal como avisos de serviço, mensagens administrativas e a Newsletter BeWelcome que são considerados como parte da sua conta BeWelcome. Se quiser optar por não receber certas mensagens, aceda à sua conta BeWelcome e vá às suas Preferências clicando na ligação para a conta no canto superior direito. Nessa página pode alterar as suas preferências. Se quiser apagar a sua conta, aceda ao BeWelcome, vá a Minha conta > Alterar perfil. Na coluna da esquerda há uma opção \'apagar perfil\'. clique, preencha alguma informação opcional no formulário, marque a caixa de verificação ao fundo e clique no botão \'Apagar Perfil\'.</p> <h4>Confidencialidade e Segurança</h4><p>Limitamos o acesso a informação pessoal sobre si aos funcionários e entidades terceiras que acreditamos precisarem do acesso a essa informação para lhe oferecer produtos ou serviços ou para realizar os seus trabalhos. \r\nTemos seguranças físicas, eletrónicas e procedimentais para proteger Informação Pessoal sobre si e a sua conta BeWelcome. Estão ainda protegidos por uma senha de acesso escolhida por si. O BeWelcome usa encriptação SSL em certas áreas do Website para proteger o envio de dados. No entanto, nenhuma companhia, incluindo a BeWelcome, pode eliminar completamente os riscos associados à Informação Pessoal. </p><h4>Outros Sites</h4><p>O facto de apresentarmos ligações para outros sites destina-se apenas à sua própria conveniência e não significa que apoiemos esses sites ou o seu conteúdo. Não temos qualquer controlo, nem fiscalizamos, nem podemos ser responsabilizados por estes websites externos ou pelo seu conteúdo. Tenha em atenção que os termos desta Política de Privacidade não se aplicam a sites de terceiros.</p><h4>Contacte-nos</h4><p>Caso tenha questões ou preocupações acerca desta Política de Privacidade, por favor contacte-nos:\r\n<address>BeVolunteer 19 rue de Paris 35500 Vitré FRANÇA</address> </p><h4>Alterações a esta Política de Privacidade</h4><p>O BeWelcome pode atualizar esta política de tempos a tempos. Notificá-lo/a-emos sempre que houver alterações significativas na forma como tratamos Informação Pessoal, enviando um aviso para o endereço de correio eletrónico indicado na sua conta BeWelcome ou colocando um aviso bem visível no nosso Website. Se se opuser a essas alterações deve deixar de usar o nosso Website. A utilização continuada do nosso Website após a notificação de alterações indica a sua concordância com as mesmas e a aceitação dos termos e condições descritos nessas alterações. </p><p>Esta Política foi atualizada pela última vez em Junho de 2012.</p>', '2014-01-03 16:38:06', '2019-04-23 18:16:49', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'yes', '', 5, NULL, 38787),
	('privacypolicy', 'sr', 'messages', '<h3>Правила приватности</h3><p>BeWelcome нуди online место за упознавање са пријатељима, и шансу да се са њима сретнете. This Privacy Policy is intended to inform you of BeWelcome\'s policies and practices regarding the collection, use and disclosure of any Personal Information you submit to us through our Website. \r\nBeWelcome ("BeWelcome", "us" or "we") respects the privacy of the visitors to its Website, the home page of which is located at http://www.BeWelcome.org ("Website"). </p><h4>Terms of this disclaimer</h4><p>"Personal Information" is information about you that is personally identifiable to you, like your name, address, e-mail address, or phone number, as well as other non-public information that is associated with the foregoing. \r\n"Anonymous Information" means information that is not associated with or linked to your Personal Information; Anonymous Information does not permit the identification of individual persons. We collect and use Personal Information and Anonymous Information as described in this Privacy Policy. </p><h4>User Consent</h4><p>By submitting Personal Information through our Website, you agree to the terms of this Privacy Policy and expressly consent to the processing of your Personal Information according to this Privacy Policy. Your Personal Information may be processed by BeWelcome in the country where it was collected as well as other countries (including the United States of America) where laws regarding processing of Personal Information may be less stringent than the laws in your country.</p><h4>General</h4><p>We collect Personal Information that you submit to us voluntarily through our Website.<ul><li> When you register for the BeWelcome network, we will collect your name, e-mail address, your gender, date of birth and post code.</li><li>When you save other Personal Information in your profile we will collect any such information you enter.</li><li>When you enter Personal Information throughout the BeWelcome network using one of the features of the BeWelcome network, for example blogs, groups, or message boards (forum), we will collect any such information you enter ("Publicly Posted Information").</li><li>When you contact us by sending us an e-mail, we will collect your e-mail addresses and any information contained in the e-mail you send us. Once you register with BeWelcome and sign in to our services, you are not anonymous to us. If you are browsing the Website without registering with BeWelcome, you are anonymous to us, but we will collect the information listed below under Personal Information Collected Via Technology.</li></ul></p> \r\n<h4>Use of information</h4><p>Any visitor of the BeWelcome website can view your profile information and photos that you have uploaded to the BeWelcome community. You can control what part of your profile information and photos is visible to visitors of the BeWelcome website and which network of BeWelcome members can see what information. To provide you with some of the features that the BeWelcome community offers to its members, we may use Personal Information that is stored in your profile after you have requested such features, for example to send invitation e-mails to people that you specified as being interested in joining the BeWelcome community. When you decide to view a member\'s profile, we may show that BeWelcome member that you chose to view their profile. If you decide to use certain features of the BeWelcome network (like blogs, groups, message boards and the like), some of the Personal Information you entered into your BeWelcome profile and any information, including Personal Information, that you enter using one of these features, might be used and displayed. BeWelcome members can use the search feature to search for other members by different criteria, like location or interests. The Personal Information that BeWelcome members enter into the BeWelcome profile will be used for these searches. Please be aware that any information that is publicly posted throughout the BeWelcome network can be accessed by every visitor of the Website. BeWelcome may analyse any collected information for its own internal purposes. BeWelcome may use Anonymous Information for any purpose and disclose Anonymous Information in its discretion.</p><h4>Information Sharing and Disclosure</h4><p>BeWelcome does not rent, sell, or share personal information about you with other people or companies except to provide products or services you\'ve requested, when we have your permission, or as otherwise described in this privacy policy. \r\nWe will disclose information in response to subpoenas, court orders, or legal process, or to establish or exercise our legal rights or defend against legal claims. We may disclose information, if we believe it is necessary to investigate, prevent, or take action regarding suspected illegal activities or fraud, situations involving the physical safety of any person, violations of BeWelcome\'s terms of use, or as otherwise required by applicable law. </p> \r\n<h4>Personal Information Collected Via Technology</h4><p>As you navigate the Website, certain information may also be passively collected and stored on our server logs, including your Internet protocol address, browser type, and operating system. We also use Cookies and navigational data like Uniform Resource Locators (URL) to gather information regarding the date and time of your visit and the solutions and information for which you searched and viewed. This type of information is collected to make our services and solutions more useful to you and to tailor the BeWelcome community experience to meet your special interests and needs. If you search the BeWelcome community by using a toolbar that BeWelcome, we may collect Anonymous Information about you automatically, but we will not collect Personal Information. \r\nAn "Internet protocol address" or "IP Address" is a number that is automatically assigned to your computer when you use the Internet. In some cases your IP Address stays the same from browser session to browser session; but if you use a consumer internet access provider, your IP Address probably varies from session to session. We track your IP Address when you login to the Website. \r\n"Cookies" are small pieces of information that a web site sends to your computer\'s hard drive while you are viewing a web site. BeWelcome may use both session Cookies (which expire once you close your web browser) and persistent Cookies (which stay on your computer until you delete them) to provide you with a more personal and interactive experience on the Website. Persistent Cookies can be removed by following your Internet browser help file directions. If you choose to disable Cookies, some areas of the Website may not work properly. Other third parties may place advertisements and cookies on webpages within the BeWelcome network. Other companies and organisations use of their cookies is subject to their own privacy policies, not this one. </p><h4>Your Ability to Edit and Delete Your Account Information and Preferences</h4><p>We reserve the right to send you certain communications relating to the BeWelcome service, such as service announcements, administrative messages and the BeWelcome Newsletter, that are considered part of your BeWelcome account. If you would like to opt out of certain messages, log into BeWelcome and go to your account settings by clicking the account link in the top right hand corner. On that page you can edit your preferences. If you would like to delete your account, log into BeWelcome, Go to My account > Edit my profile in the left column there\'s a \'delete my profile\' link, click this, then fill in some optional data in the form, and check the checkbox below, finally press the \'submit query\'.</p> <h4>Confidentiality and Security</h4><p>We limit access to personal information about you to employees and third parties who we reasonably believe need access to that information to provide products or services to you or in order to do their jobs. \r\nWe have physical, electronic, and procedural safeguards to protect personal information about you and your BeWelcome account information is protected by a password that you select. BeWelcome uses industry-standard SSL encryption in certain areas of the Website to protect data transmissions. However, no company, including BeWelcome, can fully eliminate security risks associated with Personal Information. </p><h4>Other Sites</h4><p>Our provision of a link to any other website or location is for your convenience and does not signify our endorsement of such other website or location or its contents. We have no control over, do not review, and cannot be responsible for these outside websites or their content. Please be aware that the terms of our Privacy Policy does not apply to these outside websites.</p><h4>Contact Us</h4><p>Should you have any questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact us: \r\n<address>BeVolunteer 19 rue de Paris 35500 VitrÃ© FRANCE</address> </p><h4>Измене ових правила</h4><p>BeWelcome с времена на време може да измени правила. Ми ћемо вас обавестити значајним изменама о томе као третирамо личне информације слањем обавештења на главну имејл адресу наведену у вашем профилу или постављањем упадљиве поруке на нашем сајту. If you object to any such changes, you must cease using our Website. Continued use of our Website following notice of any such changes shall indicate your acknowledgement of such changes and agreement to be bound by the terms and conditions of such changes. </p><p>Последња измена овог правила је уражена јуна 2012.</p>', '2013-03-29 19:26:57', '2019-04-23 18:16:49', '0000-00-00 00:00:00', 'yes', '', 5, NULL, 39772),
